This folder holds Evans' PolRadTran radiative transfer models RT3 and RT4
as distributed, with the changes ARTS needs.

Origin: PolRadTran.tar from https://nit.coloradolinux.com/polrad.html
(sha256 7b0eff794319330321e27a6f312588a289ed080bb266500dcecf485f6a7cff9d),
under the MIT licence in LICENSE, which must be kept with the code.  README
is Evans' description of the package.  RT3 (randomly oriented particles,
solar and thermal sources, all Fourier azimuth modes, I, Q, U and V) is
Evans and Stephens (1991), JQSRT 46, 413-423; RT4 (horizontally oriented
particles, thermal source, I and Q) is Evans and Stephens (1995), J. Atmos.
Sci. 52, 2058-2072.

Layout.  Every file of the tar is here, in one folder as in the tar.  Where
ARTS modifies a file, the modified file has the tar's name and the tar's
file is kept beside it as *.orig (radmat.f, radintg3.f, radscat3.f,
radtran3.f, radutil3.f, radintg4.f, radscat4.f, radtran4.f, radutil4.f).
All other tar files are unchanged: LICENSE, README, rt3.f, rt4.f,
scatcnv.f, runmietest, runtesta, runtestr, runtestc and cl340d14.dda.  So
the tar is the *.orig files under their own names plus the unchanged files.
New for ARTS: rt3_c_interface.f90, rt4_c_interface.f90, CMakeLists.txt and
this file.

What is built (CMakeLists.txt; ENABLE_RT3 and ENABLE_RT4, on by default when
a Fortran compiler is found):

- polradtran_radmat: radmat.f, Evans' matrix routines, shared by both
  libraries.  It differs from the tar by the rt4_ prefix on its BLAS
  helpers (rt4_daxpy, rt4_dscal, rt4_idamax, rt4_dswap), so that it cannot
  clash with a linked BLAS, and by MMULT, which calls BLAS DGEMM (ARTS's
  LAPACK libraries) instead of Evans' triple loop.  The doubling of both
  solvers spends most of its time in MMULT; the results differ from the
  loop's by the summation order only, at rounding.  It keeps no state between calls and is compiled
  with -frecursive (GNU) or -auto (Intel) so that MINVERT's local arrays are
  on the stack, because RT4 and RT3 serialise their calls with separate
  mutexes and may call it concurrently.
- rt3 and rt4: the libraries behind src/core/rt3 and src/core/rt4, from the
  modified sources and the C interfaces.
- rt3-evans, rt4-evans and scatcnv-evans: Evans' original programs rt3.f,
  rt4.f and scatcnv.f, built from the unmodified sources (the *.orig files
  and radmat.f.orig) and not linked into ARTS.  They run Evans' four
  benchmark scripts unchanged (cpp.fast.polradtran-run*, see
  src/tests/polradtran): each reproduces his expected output, the RT3
  tables to one unit in the last printed digit and the RT4 tables exactly.
  The ARTS libraries are compared with the same tables in
  cpp.fast.polradtran-rt4-arts, cpp.fast.rt3-test and
  cpp.fast.vdisort-rt3-test (with VDISORT).

The legacy *.f files are compiled with -std=legacy -fdefault-real-8
-fdefault-double-8 (GNU) or -r8 (Intel), as ARTS 2.6 compiled them.
CMake initialises CMAKE_Fortran_FLAGS from the FFLAGS environment variable
the first time Fortran is enabled in a build tree; configure with
-DCMAKE_Fortran_FLAGS="" for a reproducible build.

ARTS 2 changes to RT4 (radintg4.f, radscat4.f, radtran4.f, radutil4.f; not
marked in the source, see the diffs against the *.orig files):

- In-memory scattering properties.  RADTRANO takes NSL sets of
  EXTINCT_MATRIX, EMIS_VECTOR and SCATTER_MATRIX and the set of each layer,
  SCATLAYERS, instead of the scattering files SCAT_FILES; CHECK_NORM checks
  every set.  The extinction and emission arrays have NSTOKES (not 4) rows.
- Surfaces prepared outside RT4: the ground types S (SPECULAR_SURFACE and
  SPECULAR_RADIANCE, a fixed reflectivity applied specularly) and A
  (EXTERNAL_SURFACE, a given reflection matrix and emission), in addition to
  L and F.
- Output at every level, without the up and down fluxes (NOUTLEVELS,
  OUTLEVELS, UP_FLUX and DOWN_FLUX removed), and NUUMMU extra zero-weight
  angles.

ARTS3 changes to RT4 (each marked with a "c ARTS3:" comment in the source):

- radutil4.f PLANCK_FUNCTION: the 5-digit radiation constants 1.1911D8
  and 1.4388D4 (a ~3e-5 relative bias, ~8 mK at 250 K) are replaced by 2hc^2
  [W m-2 sr-1 um^4] and hc/k [um K] evaluated from the exact SI (CODATA 2018)
  h, c and k.
- radtran4.f RADTRANO: NUUMMU is declared INTEGER (it was implicitly
  typed), and UP_RAD/DOWN_RAD are declared with their written extent
  NSTOKES*NUMMU*(NUM_LAYERS+1).
- rt4_c_interface.f90 (new): ISO_C_BINDING entry points with explicit C
  types for RADTRANO, PLANCK_FUNCTION and the three quadratures, so the build
  needs neither -fdefault-integer-8 nor the hidden CHARACTER length ABI.
  It also has an entry point for every other subroutine RADTRANO calls
  (INITIALIZE, INITIAL_SOURCE, NONSCATTER_LAYER, DOUBLING_INTEGRATION,
  COMBINE_LAYERS, INTERNAL_RADIANCE, the LAMBERT_, FRESNEL_, SPECULAR_ and
  EXTERNAL_SURFACE/_RADIANCE routines, THERMAL_RADIANCE, and MCOPY, MZERO
  and MIDENTITY of radmat.f).  ARTS's RT4 is the C++ port of RADTRANO and
  of all these routines (src/core/rt4/radtran4.cc, radintg4.cc and
  radutil4.cc) and calls no Fortran.  It uses ARTS's quadratures instead
  of the three quadrature routines, ARTS's planck() in SI instead of
  PLANCK_FUNCTION, ARTS's fresnel() and rtepack for the Fresnel ground, and
  matpack and BLAS/LAPACK instead of radmat.f, and it takes the ground as
  external data (ground type A) for every kind of ground.  The Fortran
  RADTRANO and these entry points stay in librt4 as the reference that
  cpp.fast.rt4-radtrano-test compares the port with.

Nothing else is changed in RT4 beyond the ARTS 2 changes above; in
particular SYMMETRIC stays .TRUE., so RT4 only handles media that are mirror
symmetric between the two hemispheres.

ARTS3 changes to RT3 (each marked with a "c ARTS3:" comment in the source):

- In-memory scattering properties (radtran3.f, radscat3.f).  RADTRAN takes
  NSL scattering sets (SCAT_EXTINCT, SCAT_SCATTER, SCAT_NLEGEN and
  SCAT_COEF(6,LDCOEF,NSL), the six columns of a scattering file for
  L = 0 .. SCAT_NLEGEN) and the 1-based set of each layer, SCATLAYERS (0 for
  no scattering), instead of the file names SCAT_FILES.  Each set is
  processed once, in set order (RT3 processed every new file in layer
  order).  READ_SCAT_FILE is replaced by GET_SCAT_SET, which copies a set and
  applies READ_SCAT_FILE's delta-M scaling unchanged.  With delta-M the
  scaling reads the coefficients up to L = 2*NUMMU even when the series is
  shorter; READ_SCAT_FILE read entries there that the file never set (left
  from an earlier file, or uninitialised), GET_SCAT_SET sets them to zero.
  The check NLEGEN < MAXLEG now precedes the copy (RT3 checked
  after reading, one coefficient too late).  New STOPs: NSL > MAXLAY, and
  the direct-beam buffer for NSL sets.  The truncation message names the
  set number instead of the file.  NOUTLEVELS/OUTLEVELS are unchanged.
- Symbol clashes with RT4 (radintg3.f, radscat3.f, radutil3.f,
  radtran3.f).  The routines that RT4 also defines carry an RT3_ prefix:
  CHECK_NORM, COMBINE_LAYERS, DOUBLE_GAUSS_QUADRATURE, DOUBLING_INTEGRATION,
  FRESNEL_RADIANCE, FRESNEL_SURFACE, GAUSS_LEGENDRE_QUADRATURE, INITIALIZE,
  INITIAL_SOURCE, INTERNAL_RADIANCE, LAMBERT_RADIANCE, LAMBERT_SURFACE,
  LOBATTO_QUADRATURE, NONSCATTER_LAYER, PLANCK_FUNCTION, THERMAL_RADIANCE,
  and the COMMON blocks /SCRATCH1/ and /SCRATCH2/ are /RT3_SCRATCH1/ and
  /RT3_SCRATCH2/ (with the same names, RT3 and RT4 would share the scratch
  memory).  Two calls are wrapped onto a continuation line to stay within
  column 72; no original code line extends beyond column 72.  librt3 and
  librt4 export no common symbol.
- radutil3.f RT3_PLANCK_FUNCTION: the 5-digit radiation constants 1.1911D8
  and 1.4388D4 are replaced by the exact-SI values used in RT4.  At 3 um
  and 300-200 K this raises B by 2.1e-4 to 3.4e-4 relative.
- rt3_c_interface.f90 (new): rt3_radtran and the three quadratures with
  explicit C types (int64_t scalars and index arrays, one-character flags by
  value, the complex ground index as two doubles).

Nothing else is changed.  The remaining STOPs (array limits, the Legendre
normalisation check, the FFT size) are checked by the C++ wrapper before
the call; see src/core/rt3/rt3.h and doc/arts/dev.rt3.rst.
